# r15 DIAGNOSTIC + FRICTION - B9c/B10: a top-level condition on a build constant the command line did not define
# says "this top-level condition uses what exists only in the branches it decides, or does not check" - nothing about
# 'Profile' being unknown, or about '-D Profile=...'. Later uses say "unknown name 'Profile'". And there is no way to
# give a build constant a default (C's #ifndef, Go's -ldflags -X over a declared variable): declaring "Profile :=
# "dev"" is B10's "'Profile' is a build constant - choose another name" whenever -D does define it. Found writing
# ../config.olang, which therefore cannot be built without "-D Profile=...".
#
# expected: "unknown name 'Profile' - a build constant is defined with -D Profile=VALUE" (and some way to default it)
# actual:   error[B9c] as quoted, then "unknown name 'Profile'" at the println
if Profile == "prod" {
    Port := 443
} else {
    Port := 8080
}

fn main() ? {
    println($Profile " " $Port)
}
